    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11184" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏrĭŏli</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κορίολα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Latium, destroyed by Caius
				Marcius</i>, who, on account of this, received the surname
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏrĭŏlānus</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">Liv. 2, 33, 5 sq.</span></i>—In
				plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏrĭŏlāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Corioli</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5,
				9, § 69</span></i>.</div>
